  "_about": "a mute swan afloat (swim.depth: the waterline at y = .18): a long full boat of a body, the wings held a little raised over the back with the primaries crossing over the short pointed tail, the neck in its S rising from the breast, the head held level with the bill pointing down, orange bill with the black knob, lores and nail -- aloft (the viewer's fly) the folded wings turn into the body and a broad white spread wing swings out feather by feather (swan.py, nbwing.aloft) (2026-11-08, swanneck.py) Aloft the neck is held STRAIGHT out, drooping a little, the head level on it: its upper tube split at the bend onto a third bone (neck3) so each piece turns onto one line (it dipped off the breast and rose in a hump: an S). (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
